# Testing rules (CI parity)

## Hard gate
- The only valid test command is:
  `npm test`
- It runs `node --test tests/` (Node built-in test runner).
- This command must pass before declaring work done.

## When changing behavior
- Any behavior change requires adding/updating tests under `tests/` (`*.test.js`).
- Any bug fix requires a regression test.

## Node/Express specifics
- Use `supertest` for HTTP-level tests against the Express app.
- Tests rely on the same `sql.js` SQLite the app uses; keep tests isolated and deterministic. Avoid touching the production DB file (`data/forest-park.db`) — use a temp DB path or reset state.
- Prefer `node --test` style (`describe`/`test` from `node:test`, assertions from `node:assert/strict`).

## What NOT to do
- Do not introduce other test runners or commands (no `pytest`, `jest`, `mocha`, `vitest`, `pnpm`, `yarn`, Makefile-based gates).
- Do not add flaky time-based sleeps; prefer dependency injection / mocking where needed.
